A command whose functions each hold a type error and carry a record naming a code
no finding about a function can carry: a code about a record, a file or a
dependency, codes Go never reports, and declaration codes about an enum member or
an interface. Each record is stale although the type error skips its function.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

//deadset:ignore DS9003 -- kept for the loader
func record() int { return undefinedName }

//deadset:ignore DS1601 -- kept for the loader
func file() int { return undefinedName }

//deadset:ignore DS1701 -- kept for the loader
func dependency() int { return undefinedName }

//deadset:ignore DS1004 -- kept for the loader
func binding() int { return undefinedName }

//deadset:ignore DS1801 -- kept for the loader
func schema() int { return undefinedName }

//deadset:ignore DS1005 -- kept for the loader
func enumMember() int { return undefinedName }

//deadset:ignore DS1201 -- kept for the loader
func iface() int { return undefinedName }
